AmbireRecoveryActionExecuteHandoverTest
├── when the account is a proxy over another implementation
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should leave every privilege and the attempt as they were
├── when the account accepts any call and returns nothing
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should read no attempt and call no account
├── when the account delegates to the served implementation
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should leave every privilege and the attempt as they were
├── when the account has no code
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should read no attempt and call no account
├── when no attempt was ever recorded
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should carry the attempt's state, clock and hash before any account call
├── when the attempt was cancelled
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should carry the attempt's state, clock and hash before any account call
├── when the attempt was consumed
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should carry the attempt's state, clock and hash before any account call
├── when the payload hashes to another commitment
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should carry the attempt's state, clock and hash before any account call
├── when the attempt is read
│   └── it should read stateOf for the account and this action
├── when the new key is zero
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should carry the payload
├── when the removed key is zero
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should carry the payload
├── when an address word carries high bits
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should carry the payload
├── when the payload carries a trailing byte
│   ├── it should hand the account the batch the decoded addresses give
│   └── it should be refused by the account's check at index 1
├── when the order has no amount
│   └── it should hand the account consume, grant and revoke under the kit signature
├── when the wait ends this second
│   └── it should hand the account the batch
├── when the order pays a token
│   └── it should add a raw token transfer to the payee
├── when the order names a token but no amount
│   └── it should hand the account consume, grant and revoke only
├── when the order pays the native asset
│   └── it should add a value call to the payee with no data
├── when the account refuses the batch
│   └── it should revert
├── when the live account runs the approved batch
│   └── it should consume the attempt, install the new key at 1 and zero the removed key
├── when the live order pays a token
│   └── it should pay the payee the amount in the token
├── when the live order pays the native asset
│   └── it should pay the payee the amount in the native asset
├── when the live open order pays the caller
│   └── it should pay the caller
├── when the live token answers false
│   └── it should complete the handover and pay nobody
├── when the live order token has no code
│   └── it should complete the handover and move no balance
├── when the live order token returns no data
│   └── it should complete the handover and move no balance
├── when the live payee refuses the payment
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should undo the whole batch and leave the attempt waiting
├── when a live payee calls the account again with the same batch
│   └── it should refuse the nested run and complete the outer one once
├── when the same live handover runs a second time
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should refuse it as a consumed attempt
├── when the live new key already holds a privilege
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should undo the whole batch with AlreadyPrivileged
└── when the live removed key holds no key value
    ├── it should revert
    └── it should undo the whole batch with NotAKey
